•	Extract IP addresses associated with failed logins and determine the unique IPs.
grep -i "Failed login" security_log.txt | grep -Eo '([0-9]{1,3}\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}' | sort -V -u

•	Extract usernames involved in failed logins, convert them to uppercase, and remove duplicate values.
grep -i "Failed login" security_log.txt | grep -Eo 'user [[:alnum:]_]+' | awk '{print $2}' | tr '[:lower:]' '[:upper:]' | sort -u

•	Find all lines containing Domain accessed, extract only the domain names, and convert them to lowercase.
grep "Domain accessed" security_log.txt | grep -Eo '([[:alnum:]-]+\.)+[[:alpha:]]{2,}' | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]'

•	Find all lines containing MD5=, extract only the MD5 hash values, and convert hexadecimal letters to uppercase.
grep "MD5=" security_log.txt | grep -Eo 'MD5=[[:xdigit:]]{32}' | cut -d= -f2 | tr '[:lower:]' '[:upper:]'

•	Find entries containing User-Agent:, extract the user-agent field, and convert it to lowercase.
